---
number: 272
title: Have I Need of Aught, O Saviour!
author: Corie F. Davis
composer: W. O. Perkins
sp_category: "20"
topic: Faith and Trust
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Have I need of aught,
O Saviour! Aught on earth but Thee?
Have I any in the heavens,
Any one but Thee?

[chorus]
Only Thee, only Thee,
O the wondrous love shown me!
Only Thee, only Thee,
None on earth but Thee.

[verse 2]
Though I have of friends so many,
Love, and gold, and health,
If I have not Thee, my Saviour,
Hold I any wealth?

[chorus]
Only Thee, only Thee,
O the wondrous love shown me!
Only Thee, only Thee,
None on earth but Thee.

[verse 3]
Is there heart so kind and patient
With my failings all?
Or a voice so true and ready,
Answering my call?

[chorus]
Only Thee, only Thee,
O the wondrous love shown me!
Only Thee, only Thee,
None on earth but Thee.

[verse 4]
Not for worlds would I exchange it
This sweet faith in Thee!
Earthly treasures cannot equal
All Thou art to me.

[chorus]
Only Thee, only Thee,
O the wondrous love shown me!
Only Thee, only Thee,
None on earth but Thee.
